ung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1016":1834,"1017":"have","1018":"I practise English every day.","1019":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1020":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":37.5,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":3,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":true,"details":[{"questionId":1016,"question_id":1016,"question_content":"Had I known about the delay, I ___ earlier.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1834,"selected_answer":"would have left","correctAnswerId":1834,"correct_answer":"would have left","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đảo ngữ điều kiện loại ba: Had + S + V3, S + would have + V3.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1017,"question_id":1017,"question_content":"Had she known, she would ___ helped.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"have","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"have","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: have. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1018,"question_id":1018,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoà