(178,34,11,128,NULL,N'exercise',N'Learning beyond the classroom · Writing & speaking',N'graded',DATEADD(MINUTE,5,DATEADD(DAY,-27,@SeedNow)),NULL,DATEADD(MINUTE,12,DATEADD(DAY,-27,@SeedNow)),N'[{"id":636,"exercise_id":128,"content":"He said that he ___ tired.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"explanation":"Khi tường thuật với said ở quá khứ, am/is thường lùi thành was.","correct_text":"","order_index":1,"answers":[{"id":1149,"question_id":636,"content":"is","is_correct":0},{"id":1150,"question_id":636,"content":"was","is_correct":1},{"id":1151,"question_id":636,"content":"has","is_correct":0},{"id":1152,"question_id":636,"content":"were","is_correct":0}]},{"id":637,"exercise_id":128,"content":"She said she ___ studying English. (be)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"explanation":"Đáp án: was. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","correct_text":"was","order_index":2,"answers":[]},{"id":638,"exercise_id":128,"content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"explanation":"Câu khẳng định: chủ ngữ + động từ + tân ngữ + trạng ngữ. Chấp nhận có hoặc không có dấu chấm.","correct_text":"I practise English every day.|I practise English every day","order_index":3,"answers":[]},{"id":639,"exercise_id":128,"content":"Write 120–180 words about “Learning beyond the classroom”. Give an opinion and two supporting examples.","type":"essay","points":3,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: hoàn thành yêu cầu, tổ chức ý, từ vựng và ngữ pháp. Giáo viên đọc bài và phản hồi; không chấm chỉ bằng độ dài.","correct_text":"","order_index":4,"answers":[]},{"id":640,"exercise_id":128,"content":"Speak for one minute about “Learning beyond the classroom”. Give your opinion and one example. Submit a transcript or a recording link.","type":"speaking","points":2,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: mạch lạc, từ vựng, cấu trúc và phát âm nếu có bản ghi âm. Với bản chép lời, giáo viên chỉ nhận xét nội dung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"636":1150,"637":"was","638":"I practise English every day.","639":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","640":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":93.75,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":7.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":636,"question_id":636,"question_content":"He said that he ___ tired.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1150,"selected_answer":"was","correctAnswerId":1150,"correct_answer":"was","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Khi tường thuật với said ở quá khứ, am/is thường lùi thành was.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":637,"question_id":637,"question_content":"She said she ___ studying English. (be)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"was","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"was","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: was. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":638,"question_id":638,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_a