ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1786":3221,"1787":"on","1788":"incorrect sample answer","1789":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1790":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":25,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":2,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":true,"details":[{"questionId":1786,"question_id":1786,"question_content":"The proposal was rejected on the ___ that it lacked evidence.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":3221,"selected_answer":"grounds","correctAnswerId":3221,"correct_answer":"grounds","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Cụm cố định on the grounds that nghĩa là với lý do rằng.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1787,"question_id":1787,"question_content":"The conclusion is based ___ the available evidence.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"on","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"on|upon","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: on hoặc upon. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1788,"question_id":1788,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu h