{"1876":3382,"1877":"went","1878":"I practise English every day.","1879":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1880":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":93.75,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":7.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1876,"question_id":1876,"question_content":"We visited our grandparents ___.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":3382,"selected_answer":"yesterday","correctAnswerId":3382,"correct_answer":"yesterday","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Quá khứ đơn visited phù hợp với yesterday.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1877,"question_id":1877,"question_content":"Yesterday, I ___ to school. (go)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"went","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"went","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: went. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1878,"question_id":1878,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_a