,"answers":[]}]',N'{"106":197,"107":"played","108":"incorrect sample answer","109":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","110":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":81.25,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":6.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":106,"question_id":106,"question_content":"Despite ___ tired, she finished the task.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":197,"selected_answer":"being","correctAnswerId":197,"correct_answer":"being","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Sau despite dùng danh từ hoặc V-ing, không dùng mệnh đề độc lập.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":107,"question_id":107,"question_content":"Despite the rain, they ___ outside. (play, past)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"played","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"played","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: played. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":108,"question_id":108,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering",