text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"866":1565,"867":"incorrect sample answer","868":"I practise English every day.","869":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","870":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":25,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":2,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":true,"details":[{"questionId":866,"question_id":866,"question_content":"It is essential that the data ___ checked carefully.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1565,"selected_answer":"be","correctAnswerId":1565,"correct_answer":"be","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Cấu trúc giả định sau essential/recommend dùng động từ nguyên mẫu.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":867,"question_id":867,"question_content":"The committee recommended that he ___ present.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"incorrect sample answer","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"be","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Đáp án: be. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":0,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":868,"question_id":868,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn c