viên chỉ nhận xét nội dung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"936":1690,"937":"more confident","938":"I practise English every day.","939":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","940":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":84.38,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":6.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":936,"question_id":936,"question_content":"The more precisely we define the problem, ___ the solution becomes.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1690,"selected_answer":"the clearer","correctAnswerId":1690,"correct_answer":"the clearer","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"So sánh kép: the + comparative..., the + comparative...","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":937,"question_id":937,"question_content":"The more you practise, the ___ you become. (confident)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"more confident","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"more confident","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: more confident. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false}