ung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1006":1817,"1007":"on","1008":"incorrect sample answer","1009":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1010":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":71.88,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":5.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1006,"question_id":1006,"question_content":"The proposal was rejected on the ___ that it lacked evidence.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1817,"selected_answer":"grounds","correctAnswerId":1817,"correct_answer":"grounds","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Cụm cố định on the grounds that nghĩa là với lý do rằng.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1007,"question_id":1007,"question_content":"The conclusion is based ___ the available evidence.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"on","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"on|upon","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: on hoặc upon. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1008,"question_id":1008,"question_content":"Sắp xếp cá