{"1836":3312,"1837":"taller","1838":"I practise English every day.","1839":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1840":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":93.75,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":7.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1836,"question_id":1836,"question_content":"This bag is ___ than that one.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":3312,"selected_answer":"cheaper","correctAnswerId":3312,"correct_answer":"cheaper","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Tính từ ngắn cheap có dạng so sánh hơn cheaper.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1837,"question_id":1837,"question_content":"My brother is ___ than me. (tall)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"taller","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"taller","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: taller. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1838,"question_id":1838,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"se