s":[]}]',N'{"1536":2770,"1537":"was","1538":"I practise English every day.","1539":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1540":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":37.5,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":3,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":true,"details":[{"questionId":1536,"question_id":1536,"question_content":"He said that he ___ tired.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":2770,"selected_answer":"was","correctAnswerId":2770,"correct_answer":"was","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Khi tường thuật với said ở quá khứ, am/is thường lùi thành was.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1537,"question_id":1537,"question_content":"She said she ___ studying English. (be)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"was","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"was","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: was. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1538,"question_id":1538,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":nul