t":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"316":574,"317":"sufficient","318":"I practise English every day.","319":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","320":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":93.75,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":7.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":316,"question_id":316,"question_content":"The findings should be interpreted with ___.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":574,"selected_answer":"caution","correctAnswerId":574,"correct_answer":"caution","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Sau giới từ with cần danh từ caution; cautious là tính từ.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":317,"question_id":317,"question_content":"The evidence is not ___ to prove the claim. (suffice)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"sufficient","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"sufficient","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: sufficient. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":318,"question_id":318,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every