618":"I practise English every day.","619":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","620":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":84.38,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":6.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":616,"question_id":616,"question_content":"I have lived here ___ 2020.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1115,"selected_answer":"since","correctAnswerId":1115,"correct_answer":"since","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Since dùng với mốc thời gian; for dùng với khoảng thời gian.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":617,"question_id":617,"question_content":"She has worked here ___ five years.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"for","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"for","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: for. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":618,"question_id":618,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"I practise English ever