:"reading","1428":"incorrect sample answer","1429":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1430":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":71.88,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":5.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1426,"question_id":1426,"question_content":"They are ___ football now.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":2573,"selected_answer":"playing","correctAnswerId":2573,"correct_answer":"playing","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Hiện tại tiếp diễn có dạng be + V-ing.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1427,"question_id":1427,"question_content":"I am ___ a book now. (read)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"reading","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"reading","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: reading. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1428,"question_id":1428,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"incorrect sample answer