'{"1886":3401,"1887":"incorrect sample answer","1888":"I practise English every day.","1889":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1890":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":71.88,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":5.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1886,"question_id":1886,"question_content":"Could I ___ a cup of tea, please?","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":3401,"selected_answer":"have","correctAnswerId":3401,"correct_answer":"have","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Sau động từ khuyết thiếu could dùng động từ nguyên mẫu.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1887,"question_id":1887,"question_content":"She can ___ very well. (swim)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"incorrect sample answer","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"swim","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Đáp án: swim. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":0,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1888,"question_id":1888,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","po