(628,91,24,286,NULL,N'exercise',N'Food and everyday choices · Writing & speaking',N'graded',DATEADD(MINUTE,5,DATEADD(DAY,-26,@SeedNow)),NULL,DATEADD(MINUTE,12,DATEADD(DAY,-26,@SeedNow)),N'[{"id":1426,"exercise_id":286,"content":"They are ___ football now.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"explanation":"Hiện tại tiếp diễn có dạng be + V-ing.","correct_text":"","order_index":1,"answers":[{"id":2571,"question_id":1426,"content":"play","is_correct":0},{"id":2572,"question_id":1426,"content":"plays","is_correct":0},{"id":2573,"question_id":1426,"content":"playing","is_correct":1},{"id":2574,"question_id":1426,"content":"played","is_correct":0}]},{"id":1427,"exercise_id":286,"content":"I am ___ a book now. (read)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"explanation":"Đáp án: reading. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","correct_text":"reading","order_index":2,"answers":[]},{"id":1428,"exercise_id":286,"content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"explanation":"Câu khẳng định: chủ ngữ + động từ + tân ngữ + trạng ngữ. Chấp nhận có hoặc không có dấu chấm.","correct_text":"I practise English every day.|I practise English every day","order_index":3,"answers":[]},{"id":1429,"exercise_id":286,"content":"Write 60–90 words about “Food and everyday choices”. Give an opinion and two supporting examples.","type":"essay","points":3,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: hoàn thành yêu cầu, tổ chức ý, từ vựng và ngữ pháp. Giáo viên đọc bài và phản hồi; không chấm chỉ bằng độ dài.","correct_text":"","order_index":4,"answers":[]},{"id":1430,"exercise_id":286,"content":"Speak for one minute about “Food and everyday choices”. Give your opinion and one example. Submit a transcript or a recording link.","type":"speaking","points":2,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: mạch lạc, từ vựng, cấu trúc và phát âm nếu có bản ghi âm. Với bản chép lời, giáo viên chỉ nhận xét nội dung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1426":2573,"1427":"reading","1428":"incorrect sample answer","1429":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1430":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":71.88,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":5.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1426,"question_id":1426,"question_content":"They are ___ football now.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":2573,"selected_answer":"playing","correctAnswerId":2573,"correct_answer":"playing","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Hiện tại tiếp diễn có dạng be + V-ing.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1427,"question_id":1427,"question_content":"I am ___ a book now. (read)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"reading","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"reading","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: reading. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1428,"question_id":1428,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"incorrect sample answer","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"I practise English every day.|I practise English every day","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Câu khẳng định: chủ ngữ + động từ + tân ngữ + trạng ngữ. Chấp nhận có hoặc không có dấu chấm.","earnedPoints":0,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1429,"question_id":1429,"question_content":"Write 60–90 words about “Food and everyday choices”. Give an opinion and two supporting examples.","type":"essay","points":3,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: hoàn thành yêu cầu, tổ chức ý, từ vựng và ngữ pháp. Giáo viên đọc bài và phản hồi; không chấm chỉ bằng độ dài.","earnedPoints":2.25,"needs_grading":false,"teacher_feedback":"Ý rõ và có ví dụ. Tiếp tục sửa cách liên kết câu và dùng từ chính xác hơn."},{"questionId":1430,"question_id":1430,"question_content":"Speak for one minute about “Food and everyday choices”. Give your opinion and one example. Submit a transcript or a recording link.","type":"speaking","points":2,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly.","co