rder_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1586":2861,"1587":"incorrect sample answer","1588":"I practise English every day.","1589":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1590":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":25,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":2,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":true,"details":[{"questionId":1586,"question_id":1586,"question_content":"The person ___ helped me is a teacher.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":2861,"selected_answer":"who","correctAnswerId":2861,"correct_answer":"who","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Who là đại từ quan hệ chỉ người, làm chủ ngữ.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1587,"question_id":1587,"question_content":"This is the book ___ I told you about.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"incorrect sample answer","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"that|which","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Đáp án: that hoặc which. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":0,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1588,"question_id":1588,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / En