(657,95,28,332,NULL,N'exercise',N'Making a reasoned decision · Writing & speaking',N'graded',DATEADD(MINUTE,5,DATEADD(DAY,-34,@SeedNow)),NULL,DATEADD(MINUTE,12,DATEADD(DAY,-34,@SeedNow)),N'[{"id":1656,"exercise_id":332,"content":"The more precisely we define the problem, ___ the solution becomes.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"explanation":"So sánh kép: the + comparative..., the + comparative...","correct_text":"","order_index":1,"answers":[{"id":2985,"question_id":1656,"content":"clearer","is_correct":0},{"id":2986,"question_id":1656,"content":"the clearer","is_correct":1},{"id":2987,"question_id":1656,"content":"clearest","is_correct":0},{"id":2988,"question_id":1656,"content":"most clear","is_correct":0}]},{"id":1657,"exercise_id":332,"content":"The more you practise, the ___ you become. (confident)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"explanation":"Đáp án: more confident. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","correct_text":"more confident","order_index":2,"answers":[]},{"id":1658,"exercise_id":332,"content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"explanation":"Câu khẳng định: chủ ngữ + động từ + tân ngữ + trạng ngữ. Chấp nhận có hoặc không có dấu chấm.","correct_text":"I practise English every day.|I practise English every day","order_index":3,"answers":[]},{"id":1659,"exercise_id":332,"content":"Write 120–180 words about “Making a reasoned decision”. Give an opinion and two supporting examples.","type":"essay","points":3,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: hoàn thành yêu cầu, tổ chức ý, từ vựng và ngữ pháp. Giáo viên đọc bài và phản hồi; không chấm chỉ bằng độ dài.","correct_text":"","order_index":4,"answers":[]},{"id":1660,"exercise_id":332,"content":"Speak for one minute about “Making a reasoned decision”. Give your opinion and one example. Submit a transcript or a recording link.","type":"speaking","points":2,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: mạch lạc, từ vựng, cấu trúc và phát âm nếu có bản ghi âm. Với bản chép lời, giáo viên chỉ nhận xét nội dung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1656":2986,"1657":"more confident","1658":"I practise English every day.","1659":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1660":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":93.75,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":7.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1656,"question_id":1656,"question_content":"The more precisely we define the problem, ___ the solution becomes.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":2986,"selected_answer":"the clearer","correctAnswerId":2986,"correct_answer":"the clearer","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"So sánh kép: the + comparative..., the + comparative...","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1657,"question_id":1657,"question_content":"The more you practise, the ___ you become. (confident)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"more confident","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"more confident","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: more confident. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"need