ung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"1726":3113,"1727":"on","1728":"incorrect sample answer","1729":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","1730":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":81.25,"correctCount":2,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":6.5,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":1726,"question_id":1726,"question_content":"The proposal was rejected on the ___ that it lacked evidence.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":3113,"selected_answer":"grounds","correctAnswerId":3113,"correct_answer":"grounds","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Cụm cố định on the grounds that nghĩa là với lý do rằng.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1727,"question_id":1727,"question_content":"The conclusion is based ___ the available evidence.","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"on","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"on|upon","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: on hoặc upon. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":1728,"question_id":1728,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các