(693,99,10,116,NULL,N'exercise',N'A community library · Writing & speaking',N'graded',DATEADD(MINUTE,5,DATEADD(DAY,-27,@SeedNow)),NULL,DATEADD(MINUTE,12,DATEADD(DAY,-27,@SeedNow)),N'[{"id":576,"exercise_id":116,"content":"He said that he ___ tired.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"explanation":"Khi tường thuật với said ở quá khứ, am/is thường lùi thành was.","correct_text":"","order_index":1,"answers":[{"id":1041,"question_id":576,"content":"is","is_correct":0},{"id":1042,"question_id":576,"content":"was","is_correct":1},{"id":1043,"question_id":576,"content":"has","is_correct":0},{"id":1044,"question_id":576,"content":"were","is_correct":0}]},{"id":577,"exercise_id":116,"content":"She said she ___ studying English. (be)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"explanation":"Đáp án: was. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","correct_text":"was","order_index":2,"answers":[]},{"id":578,"exercise_id":116,"content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"explanation":"Câu khẳng định: chủ ngữ + động từ + tân ngữ + trạng ngữ. Chấp nhận có hoặc không có dấu chấm.","correct_text":"I practise English every day.|I practise English every day","order_index":3,"answers":[]},{"id":579,"exercise_id":116,"content":"Write 120–180 words about “A community library”. Give an opinion and two supporting examples.","type":"essay","points":3,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: hoàn thành yêu cầu, tổ chức ý, từ vựng và ngữ pháp. Giáo viên đọc bài và phản hồi; không chấm chỉ bằng độ dài.","correct_text":"","order_index":4,"answers":[]},{"id":580,"exercise_id":116,"content":"Speak for one minute about “A community library”. Give your opinion and one example. Submit a transcript or a recording link.","type":"speaking","points":2,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: mạch lạc, từ vựng, cấu trúc và phát âm nếu có bản ghi âm. Với bản chép lời, giáo viên chỉ nhận xét nội dung/ngôn ngữ.","correct_text":"","order_index":5,"answers":[]}]',N'{"576":1042,"577":"was","578":"I practise English every day.","579":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","580":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly."}',N'{"scorePercentage":84.38,"correctCount":3,"totalQuestions":5,"earnedPoints":6.75,"totalPoints":8,"pending_grading":false,"details":[{"questionId":576,"question_id":576,"question_content":"He said that he ___ tired.","type":"multiple_choice","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":1042,"selected_answer":"was","correctAnswerId":1042,"correct_answer":"was","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Khi tường thuật với said ở quá khứ, am/is thường lùi thành was.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":577,"question_id":577,"question_content":"She said she ___ studying English. (be)","type":"fill_blank","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"was","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"was","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Đáp án: was. Đọc lại toàn bộ câu sau khi điền.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":578,"question_id":578,"question_content":"Sắp xếp các từ thành câu hoàn chỉnh: every day / English / I / practise","type":"ordering","points":1,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"I practise English every day.","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"I practise English every day.|I practise English every day","isCorrect":true,"is_correct":true,"explanation":"Câu khẳng định: chủ ngữ + động từ + tân ngữ + trạng ngữ. Chấp nhận có hoặc không có dấu chấm.","earnedPoints":1,"needs_grading":false},{"questionId":579,"question_id":579,"question_content":"Write 120–180 words about “A community library”. Give an opinion and two supporting examples.","type":"essay","points":3,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"In my opinion, small changes can improve the way we learn and work. For example, planning a short activity every day makes a large goal easier to manage. It also helps us notice problems early. In our study group, we compare ideas and explain our answers instead of memorising a list. This is useful because a clear example often reveals what we do not understand. However, the plan should remain flexible: people have different schedules and need time to rest. I would review the plan each week and choose one thing to improve.","correctAnswerId":null,"correct_answer":"","isCorrect":false,"is_correct":false,"explanation":"Tiêu chí: hoàn thành yêu cầu, tổ chức ý, từ vựng và ngữ pháp. Giáo viên đọc bài và phản hồi; không chấm chỉ bằng độ dài.","earnedPoints":2.25,"needs_grading":false,"teacher_feedback":"Ý rõ và có ví dụ. Tiếp tục sửa cách liên kết câu và dùng từ chính xác hơn."},{"questionId":580,"question_id":580,"question_content":"Speak for one minute about “A community library”. Give your opinion and one example. Submit a transcript or a recording link.","type":"speaking","points":2,"selectedAnswerId":null,"selected_answer":"Transcript: I think this topic matters because it affects daily decisions. For example, our class tried a short discussion before each lesson. We listened to different opinions and asked for examples. I became more confident when I prepared three key words first. Next time I would speak more slowly and explain my reason clearly.","correctAns